# Prospect funding sibling

## When this applies

Use this when adding or editing an idea card in `Prospect-Businesses/`, and when writing that card's funding note. Skip `TEMPLATE.md`, `FUNDING_TEMPLATE.md`, `README.md`, and `MANUAL_TEST.md`.

## Do

- Give every idea card a sibling `{slug}-funding.md` in the same folder.
- Copy `Prospect-Businesses/FUNDING_TEMPLATE.md`.
- List own cash, debt financing, grants, customer revenue, and equity financing.
- In one plain line, equity financing means people put in cash and receive an ownership share.
- Keep percents and investor names as `(blank)` until the owner chooses them.
- A money amount may replace `(blank)` only when it is copied from a public source. Write the source name, the date, and the link beside the figure.
- If no public source is found, leave the amount `(blank)` and name the failed search.
- Point the funding note at the idea card. Keep funding details out of the idea card.
- If an idea card has no sibling, add the funding file when that card is next touched.

## Do not

- Invent amounts, percents, or investor names.
- Put the owner's own money, account, address, or phone number in the tracked funding file.
- Treat a researched lot cost as an order to sell the company.
- Treat the funding note as a second prospect on the shortlist.
- Graduate the prospect into `Started-Businesses/` from this rule.
- Create a funding file for the template, the README, or the manual test.

## Example

Bad: write a naira amount with no source.

Good: write the published pack price with the page name, the date, and the link. Percent stays `(blank)`. Investor name stays `(blank)`.
